{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"multidimensionalScalingLayout"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"edgeLength"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":" = { _ in 1 }, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"maxIterations"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"NoConvergence","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Drawing","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The distance d_ij of two vertices is their shortest-path distance with "},{"code":"edgeLength","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (hops by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default); between components it is 1 + L̄·√n, L̄ the mean edge length, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"stressMajorizationLayout()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". With B = −½ J D⁽²⁾ J (D⁽²⁾ the squared distances, J the centring"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"matrix), x is √λ₁ · v₁ and y is √λ₂ · v₂ for the two largest eigenvalues λ₁ ≥ λ₂ of B and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their unit eigenvectors (a negative eigenvalue gives 0). When the distances are Euclidean"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the plane, the drawing reproduces them exactly, up to a rigid motion. Each axis’s sign"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"makes its first entry, in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order, whose magnitude is at least 10⁻⁴ of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"largest positive. The drawing is centred on the origin. A directed graph is drawn through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"undirectedView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Torgerson, “Multidimensional scaling: I. Theory and method”, Psychometrika 17(4), 1952.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"O(n·(n + m)) for the distances by breadth-first search (O(n·m log n) by Dijkstra when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lengths differ), then O(n³) for the dense eigensystem; n² ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every edge length is positive and finite; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"least 1."}]}],"style":"note","name":"Precondition"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":" after "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":" QL iterations in all (30 n when nil), as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spectralLayout(weight:maxIterations:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"style":"note","name":"Throws"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"A drawing by classical multidimensional scaling of the shortest-path distances: the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"coordinates of the best rank-2 approximation of the doubly centred squared distances.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/multidimensionalScalingLayout(edgeLength:maxIterations:)"},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"multidimensionalScalingLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"edgeLength","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int",